**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests`
- `kit-acceptance`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`

**How to implement.** The reference kit is committed as AT-1's build writes it, once, and never by hand (001 §Q 'Section 12 creates them by running the build below once, through the app's own folder `KitProxy`, and commits the result. They are never hand-written'; 001 §1 'complete kit folders … `library/` and the raw lab files under `data/`'; .spec-md §3.13). (1) The fact `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file` in `KitAcceptanceTests`: it builds the kit (`buildOpticsMuellerKit`, steps 421-427) into a fresh run folder and compares it with the committed kit (`CommittedKit.OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, .spec-md §3.21): the two folders' relative file paths, `.oc/` left out of both, are the same set, and each file's bytes are equal: every kit file at the root, every file under `library/` and every file under `data/` (001 §Q 'every kit file and every file under `data/` and `library/`; `.oc/` excluded'). A difference fails naming the built folder's absolute path, the first differing relative path and why (missing, extra or different bytes). It reads the committed kit and writes nothing there (.spec-md §4 'Tests' data'). (2) The committed kit, created by this step once: run the fact (`kit-acceptance`, filtered to it); it fails, because `data/optics-mueller/` holds the lab files alone (step 330), and names its built folder; copy every file of that folder except those under `data/` (the committed lab files, equal by the step-421 fact) and under `.oc/` into `data/optics-mueller/`, keeping their relative paths and bytes; run the fact again, and it passes. The files are the kit file, the nine `<label>.item-json`, the forty-two `<setup>.setup-json`, the fifty-three `<experiment>.experiment-json`, `QZ-LR.study-json`, the two `QZ-LR@<stamp>.fitrun-json` and `library/`'s snapshots of the built-in entries the kit references, each `library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json` named by a GUID the built-in catalogue froze (steps 20, 35, 209), all canonical JSON with LF line endings, which `.gitattributes`' `* text=auto eol=lf` keeps byte-identical; `git check-ignore` matches none of them, and `/data/*/.oc/` stays ignored (.spec-md §10.6). Nothing under `data/optics-mueller/data/` changes. (3) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha on `data/` (the last bullet of 'Gotchas'), one bullet of at most four lines: **The reference kits are AT-1's and AT-2's output, never hand-edited** (`KitAcceptanceTests.fs`, spec 0050 S12): `data/optics-mueller/` is exactly what the AT-1 build writes, `.oc/` aside; a change to what the build writes (a kit-file shape, a snapshotted catalogue entry, the build's messages) re-runs `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file` and re-commits the kit files it names in the same step. Nothing else in the file changes.

**Acceptance.** After the kit is committed, `data/optics-mueller/` MUST hold, beside its unchanged lab files, exactly the kit files and library snapshots AT-1's build writes, and `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file` MUST pass; AGENTS.md MUST carry the reference-kit gotcha; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.
